gaEn(){return"- Encrypted connections (HTTPS / TLS) between the app and the server.\n- Each company's data isolated by database access rules (RLS): users only see the companies they belong to.\n- Two-factor authentication available, enforced by the server once enabled.\n- Passwords stored hashed by the authentication service.\n- Append-only activity log: creation, change, issue, download, with IP address (erased after 12 months).\n- Bank details encrypted in the database, key stored in the Supabase Vault; each display is logged.\n- Accountant access chosen by the owner: full, read-only or none.\n- Automatic sign-out after inactivity; offline data erased at sign-out.\n- Retention periods applied automatically every night.\n- Hosting, backups and encryption at rest: see the subprocessor list."},
aEj(a,b,c,d){return a+" processes your data (identity, contact details, tax identifiers, amounts) to issue quotes, invoices, credit notes and reminders, and to meet its accounting and tax obligations. This data is intended for "+a+", its accountant and its invoicing provider eFatoura. Accounting records are kept for "+b+" months. Under Law 09-08, you have the right to access, correct and object, which you can exercise with "+a+c+". "+d},
